OmniSim and OmniLink Brand Assets — Copyright and Licence
=========================================================

Copyright 2026 OmniLink. All rights reserved.

THIS DIRECTORY IS NOT COVERED BY THE APACHE LICENSE 2.0.

Everything under resources/branding/ — the OmniSim and OmniLink logos, the
dot-sphere orb, the wordmarks, the lockups, the glyphs and favicons, and the
brand palette and trade dress they express — is the copyrighted artwork of
OmniLink and is EXCLUDED from the Apache-2.0 grant in the repository root
LICENSE file. No right to reproduce, modify, or redistribute this artwork is
granted by that licence, by this file, or by your possession of a copy of
OmniSim.

This is the ordinary arrangement for an open-source project with a protected
brand — Mozilla, Rust, Docker and the Linux Foundation all reserve their logo
copyright separately from the licence on their code — and it exists so that a
fork of OmniSim's code cannot present itself as OmniSim.

TWO DISTINCT RIGHTS, AND WHY BOTH ARE STATED
--------------------------------------------

  * COPYRIGHT in these files. That is what this notice reserves. It governs
    copying, modifying and redistributing the artwork itself.

  * TRADEMARK in the marks the artwork depicts. That is governed by the
    project's Trademark Policy in TRADEMARKS.md at the repository root, and by
    Apache-2.0 Section 6, which withholds trademark rights from the code grant.
    It governs using the marks to identify a product or a project.

They are separate, and reserving one does not reserve the other. Apache-2.0
Section 6 alone would leave a recipient free to copy, alter and republish these
image files so long as they did not use them AS marks. That is not the intent,
and this notice is what says so.

WHAT YOU MAY DO ANYWAY
----------------------

The permissions in TRADEMARKS.md apply here too, and they are deliberately
generous. In particular you may reproduce these assets UNMODIFIED to refer
factually to OmniSim or OmniLink — in an article, a talk, a course, a
compatibility badge, a screenshot, or documentation for something you built on
OmniSim. You do not need to ask. Read TRADEMARKS.md for the full statement of
what is permitted, what requires written permission, and how to ask.

What you may not do is alter these files, incorporate them into another
project's identity, or ship them as the branding of a modified distribution.
A fork that redistributes modified OmniSim code must rename and rebrand, which
means replacing everything in this directory with its own artwork — see the
"What requires written permission" section of TRADEMARKS.md.

EXCEPTIONS INSIDE THIS DIRECTORY
--------------------------------

Two things here are NOT ours and carry their own terms, which govern instead:

  * resources/branding/omnilink/fonts/Montserrat-*.ttf / *.otf — the Montserrat
    typeface, SIL Open Font License 1.1. Licence text is in the same directory
    at LICENSE-Montserrat-OFL-1.1.txt.

  * resources/branding/omnilink/fonts/Hogira-*.otf — a display typeface with no
    redistribution grant we could establish. These files are NOT part of the
    public distribution; they are removed by the release deny-list and you
    should not have them. If you do, they are not licensed to you by us. See
    the Carve-Out section of the repository root NOTICE file, and
    resources/branding/omnilink/BRAND.md, which tells a public reader which
    OFL-licensed family to substitute.

QUESTIONS
---------

Permission requests and questions about brand use: see the contact section of
TRADEMARKS.md at the repository root.
